            <exercise id="fbc3e043-7ebc-4cf4-92f8-54248608bc2a" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00018">
                  <para id="para-00092">\(3x^2−5x+1=0\)</para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00018">
                  <para id="para-00093">Correct! \(x=\frac{5}{6}+\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\), \(x=\frac{5}{6}-\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00094">Try again. Revisit activities 9.6.3 and 9.6.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00095">The correct answers are: \(x=\frac{5}{6}+\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\), \(x=\frac{5}{6}-\frac{\sqrt{13}}{6}\).</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
